cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Mosaic (mosaic-behavior)"
message: >-
  If you use mosaic in your work, cite the tools that produced the science
  first, as their authors ask (NOTICE lists them), and cite mosaic second,
  as the platform that organized the data and the runs. Cite the version
  recorded in the run's params.json as _mosaic_version.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Davidson
    given-names: Jacob
    affiliation: "Max Planck Institute of Animal Behavior"
  - family-names: Nuehrenberg
    given-names: Paul
    affiliation: "Max Planck Institute of Animal Behavior"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/EcodylicScience/mosaic"
url: "https://ecodylicscience.github.io/mosaic/"
abstract: >-
  Mosaic is a platform for behavior analysis. It drives trackers (TRex, SLEAP,
  Lightning Pose, Ultralytics) or imports tracks something else already
  produced, then provides an extensible analysis framework built on the
  feature construct: individual behavioral metrics, collective motion,
  unsupervised methods, and supervised model fitting on annotated behaviors.
  A feature can be calculated on individuals, on pairs, or on all animals at
  once. Results are organized by a content-addressed scheme for run caching
  and reproducibility.
keywords:
  - animal behavior
  - pose tracking
  - behavioral features
  - ethology
  - computational ethology
